.TH UNHEADED\-AIDE 1 "2026-11-15" "unheaded 70a102c0" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
unheaded\-aide \- Run AIDE quietly: one line per check, a change reported once, a database updated only after a review.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unheaded\-aide
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
check | init | promote | review | accept <hash>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run AIDE quietly: one line per check, a change reported once, a database updated only after a review.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B check
compare the tree with the database; one line, the metrics, the state; never writes a database
.TP
.B init
build aide.db.new and print a summary to read before promote
.TP
.B promote
make aide.db.new the database
.TP
.B review
print the diff that is waiting for a review
.TP
.B accept <hash>
update the database to the reviewed diff; refused if the tree has changed since
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-aide \fISTRING\fR
the aide binary (default /usr/bin/aide)
.TP
.B \-\-config \fISTRING\fR
AIDE config (default /etc/aide/aide\-unheaded.conf)
.TP
.B \-\-db\-dir \fISTRING\fR
directory of aide.db and aide.db.new, as the config names them (default /var/lib/aide)
.TP
.B \-\-state \fISTRING\fR
directory of state.json (default /var/lib/unheaded/aide)
.TP
.B \-\-textfile\-dir \fISTRING\fR
with check: write unheaded_aide.prom here for the textfile collector
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH NOTES
check exits 0 for a clean tree and for a detected change (the change is in the line, the metrics and
the state), 1 when AIDE could not run or its report could not be read. unheaded_aide_exit_code is AIDE's:
0 clean, 1\-7 change bits, 14 and above its errors; 99 the report could not be read, 127 aide did not start.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
unheaded\-aide check \-\-textfile\-dir /var/lib/unheaded/textfile
sudo unheaded\-aide init && sudo unheaded\-aide promote
sudo unheaded\-aide review
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
